Start the program.
Accept the number of buildings and pathways.
Initialize an adjacency matrix with all elements set to zero.
Accept the pathways between buildings and mark the corresponding matrix entries as 1.
Display the adjacency matrix.
Accept two building numbers and check whether a direct pathway exists between them.
Add a new building by increasing the number of vertices and updating the matrix.
Remove a selected pathway by setting its corresponding matrix entries to 0.
Calculate the degree of each building by adding the values in its corresponding row.
Display the updated adjacency matrix and the degree of each building.
Stop the program.
